PROJECT: FLO STUDIO
MILESTONES: M6, M7, M8
ENVIRONMENT: Existing Google AI Studio project and its current Android application architecture.

IMPORTANT: This is a continuation of an existing project. Do not create a new application, replace the current architecture unnecessarily, or remove existing functionality.

==================================================
PROJECT CONTEXT
==================================================

Flo Studio is an Android-focused automatic instrumental music composition application.

The application already has implementations for M1–M5, including:

M1: Music studio foundation, landscape interface, piano roll, playback infrastructure, project persistence, and a video-recording architecture.

M2: Automatic music composition with keys, scales, BPM, time signatures, complexity settings, deterministic seeds, melody, chords, bass, rhythm, layer regeneration, and musical variations.

M3: Locally synthesized instruments, PCM audio playback, voice pooling, ADSR envelopes, reverb, and instrument sound-design controls.

M4: Creator presets, preset browsing, and locally saved custom presets.

M5: Automatic song arrangements, section planning, track gating, velocity changes, and volume automation.

The reported implementation has passed unit tests and compiled successfully. However, actual device functionality must still be validated.

The target device is:

- Device: TECNO Camon 20
- Operating system: Android 14
- RAM: 8 GB
- Processor: MediaTek Helio G85
- Graphics: Mali-G52 MC2

The project must prioritize reliability, low memory consumption, responsive interaction, and efficient local processing.

The application should work offline for its core music creation and export features wherever Android permits.

Do not introduce mandatory cloud services, subscriptions, paid APIs, large machine-learning models, or external audio asset downloads.

