MILESTONE 8: OPTIMIZATION, BUG FIXING, AND DEVICE READINESS
==================================================

OBJECTIVE:

Make Flo Studio reliable, responsive, and usable on the Tecno Camon 20.

This milestone is not an excuse to remove complex features.

It is an engineering and validation pass over the complete application.

PART A: MEMORY OPTIMIZATION

Inspect:

- Audio voice pooling.
- Audio buffers.
- PCM rendering buffers.
- Piano-roll rendering.
- Note and event storage.
- Preset loading.
- Arrangement generation.
- WAV export.
- MIDI export.
- Video rendering.
- MediaCodec and MediaMuxer resource management.
- Temporary export files.
- Bitmap and graphics allocations.
- Activity and lifecycle cleanup.

Reduce unnecessary allocations.

Avoid allocating large buffers repeatedly inside real-time audio callbacks.

Reuse buffers where safe.

Avoid retaining full video frames in memory.

Release encoder resources and temporary files after cancellation or failure.

Prevent memory leaks when opening and closing dialogs or switching between screens.

Keep the interface responsive during long exports.

