- Audio glitches.
- Clicks and pops.
- Incorrect note timing.
- Notes that become stuck.
- Notes that end too early.
- Notes that continue after playback stops.
- Voice-pool exhaustion.
- Excessive polyphony.
- Incorrect ADSR envelopes.
- Reverb instability.
- Volume clipping.
- Incorrect track muting.
- Incorrect solo behavior.
- Instrument changes not taking effect.
- Incorrect arrangement section transitions.
- Playback scheduler drift.

Fix actual problems found in the code.

Do not arbitrarily reduce sound quality.

If polyphony limits are necessary, implement sensible limits and graceful voice stealing.

Ensure stopping playback releases active voices.

Ensure changing projects does not leave old notes playing.

Ensure the UI and audio engine agree on playback state.

